  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/pseudomystus_heokhuii_en/",
      "html": "<p>This pretty species of bumblebee catfish was discovered and scientifically described only in 2008. It has now been imported for the first time. P. heokhuii becomes about 6 cm long and is a very peaceful species of catfish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/pseudomystus_heokhuii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Pseudomystus heokhuii inhabits extreme blackwater habitats in the wild, where the pH is around 3.5-4.5.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/pseudomystus_heokhuii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Despite the extreme conditions in the wild, they adapt very well to different water conditions.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/pseudomystus_heokhuii_en/",
      "html": "<p>The females develop spawn and even in the photo tank the male showed courtship behaviour. So it seems that this pretty bumblebee catfish will even breed in aquaria.</p>"
    }
  ],
